<title>MEXICO: TMM looks for other rail opportunities.</title>
<headline>TMM looks for other rail opportunities.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transportacion Maritima Mexicana (TMM) said on Friday its rail subsidiary pulled out of the bidding for the Chiahuahua-Pacific rail concession because it was looking for railway prospects more closely tied to its business interests.</p>
<p>In a statement, TMM said Transportacion Ferroviaria Mexicana (TFM), a joint venture with Kansas City Southern, &quot;will concentrate its efforts in the other railways soon to be privatized.&quot;</p>
<p>On Wednesday, the Communications and Transport Ministry said TMM and Tribasa had voluntary withdrawn bids for the Chihuahua-Pacific line, leaving Grupo Mexico as the only bidder.</p>
<p>-- Cecilia Cardenas, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9552</p>
